FitHub Phase 3 focused evidence — DEF-004 connected equipment clearance
Execution date: 2026-10-22
Environment: local Docker Compose; Angular production container on http://localhost:4040; ASP.NET Core API and PostgreSQL containers; Development simulation endpoints enabled
Test operator role: synthetic Administrator
Synthetic Members: Elena (session-only active-membership override) and Priya (active); a third active synthetic Member was used for the sharing-capacity rejection
Equipment: Treadmill / EQ-TREADMILL-01 mapped to persisted TREAD-001
Configured clearance duration: 30 seconds

Expected result
- Claim persists as Occupied.
- Sharing persists as SharingAllowed with exactly one partner.
- A third Member is rejected without replacing the owner or partner.
- One assigned Member leaving does not start clearance while the other remains detected.
- Both assigned Members leaving starts exactly one 30-second ClearanceWarning.
- A return before expiry cancels the warning and restores SharingAllowed.
- A second uninterrupted clear period releases the machine, clears both assignments and broadcasts Available.
- Duplicate, stale and out-of-order observations do not restart or cancel the active warning.
- A transport failure is reported as backend unavailable and is never interpreted as a Member return.

Actual focused browser result
1. Connected Mode reported both API and normal EquipmentHub connected.
2. Elena claimed the treadmill: Available -> Occupied.
3. Elena enabled sharing: Occupied -> SharingAllowed.
4. Priya joined as the single sharing partner.
5. The third Member was rejected with SHARING_FULL; Elena and Priya remained displayed as the assigned Members.
6. Elena moved outside while Priya remained inside. No clearance countdown or state transition occurred.
7. Priya moved outside. One SENSOR_ZONE_EXITED and one CLEARANCE_COUNTDOWN_STARTED were recorded; the UI showed Clearance Warning and a real-time countdown from 30 seconds.
8. Priya returned before expiry. One SENSOR_ZONE_ENTERED and one CLEARANCE_COUNTDOWN_CANCELLED were recorded; SharingAllowed was restored.
9. Priya moved outside again. A new single countdown started. After 30 real seconds, one AUTOMATIC_RELEASE_COMPLETED event was accepted and the simulator displayed Available with no connected Members.
10. The event sequence contained no BACKEND_UNAVAILABLE entry and no SignalR-generated false SENSOR_ZONE_ENTERED entry.
11. With the normal Administrator equipment page open in another browser tab, a subsequent connected claim changed TREAD-001 to Occupied with owner Elena without refresh; connected reset changed it back to Available without refresh.

Persistence verification
Read-only PostgreSQL result after automatic release:
TREAD-001 | Available | OwnerUserId NULL | PartnerUserId NULL | ClearanceGraceStartedAt NULL

Automated verification
- Backend unit tests: 113 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped.
- Focused PostgreSQL SimulationApiTests: 7 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped.
- Angular suite: 40 files passed; 125 tests passed; 0 failed.
- Docker production builds: backend and frontend passed. Existing simulator component stylesheet budget warnings remain unchanged.

Decision: PASSED
Defect status: DEF-004 corrected in Phase 3. Historical Phase 2 evidence is unchanged.
